egl/surfaceless: fall back to zink without DRM devices

The surfaceless platform now also takes the device-less driver path for
zink, not only for swrast with LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE. iOS has no DRM
devices: the hardware probe finds none and the software fallback picks
swrast (not built), so surfaceless EGL never reached zink. Forcing
software rendering is no workaround either, because zink then accepts
only CPU Vulkan devices, while MoltenVK exposes the GPU. With the patch
eglInitialize retries with zink, no environment variables needed.

Upstream: not submitted.

--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c	2026-09-30 07:30:55
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c	2026-09-30 07:30:55
@@ -389,8 +389,10 @@
     */
    driver_loaded = surfaceless_probe_device(disp, disp->Options.ForceSoftware,
                                             disp->Options.Zink);
-   if (!driver_loaded && disp->Options.ForceSoftware) {
-      _eglLog(_EGL_DEBUG, "Falling back to surfaceless swrast without DRM.");
+   /* zink does not need a DRM device (e.g. Vulkan through MoltenVK on Apple platforms) */
+   if (!driver_loaded && (disp->Options.ForceSoftware || disp->Options.Zink)) {
+      _eglLog(_EGL_DEBUG, "Falling back to surfaceless %s without DRM.",
+              disp->Options.Zink ? "zink" : "swrast");
       driver_loaded = surfaceless_probe_device_sw(disp);
    }
 
